Paisa Stick is a remote-like device designed to perform cashless transactions. It transfers value from the device to other types of devices like phones, IVRs, and Android apps.

Elderly members in society find it difficult to use digital payment interfaces. How might we enable them to perform daily transactions with ease?

[Case Study ](http://rohitg.in/portfolio/works/paisa.html)

[Paper\
](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3027063.3049268)\
Citation : *Gupta, R., Vidyanta, U., & Murali, S. (2017, May). Paisa Stick: Tangible Cur- rency Interface for Cashless Transactions. In Proceedings of the 2017 CHI Conference Extended Abstracts on Human Factors in Computing Systems (pp. 60-66). ACM.*
